## LOOM, a live looper for Mac and Windows

LOOM is live looping software for macOS (Apple Silicon, macOS 13.3 or later) and Windows (Windows 10 or later, 64-bit x64). One licence covers both. It records and overdubs audio on five loop tracks like a hardware loop pedal, and loops MIDI on four instrument tracks that play its own synth, drum machine and sampler or an instrument plug-in. Its arrange view lets you draw REC, DUB and PLAY regions on a timeline, so the song presses the looper's buttons while you play over it. It has a mixer with eight insert slots per strip, built-in effects, and a compressor and noise gate that can be keyed from another track or a single drum pad. It hosts VST3 effect and instrument plug-ins on both platforms, and Audio Unit plug-ins on macOS, each in a helper process of its own outside LOOM, and draws their controls as LOOM controls, so they can be mapped to MIDI, automated in the arrange view and put on macros. It records a performance to separate synced WAV files, exports a transparent video overlay of a performed song, and makes no network calls itself. A third-party plug-in you choose to load may connect to the internet on its own, for example for its own licence check. Loops follow tempo changes, either stretched to keep their pitch or changing speed and pitch together like tape, and a render makes a clean copy at the new tempo. It is controlled from MIDI, with a built-in note layout, MIDI learn for any knob, fader, pad or footswitch, and eight macros per track that a row of knobs can play on whichever track has the focus. On macOS it sends MIDI clock to drum machines and sequencers; the Windows version does not send MIDI clock yet. It does not follow incoming clock. On Windows its keyboard shortcuts use Ctrl where the Mac uses Command. Latest version: {{ releases.latest.version }}{% if releases.latestWindows and releases.latestWindows.version != releases.latest.version %} (Windows: {{ releases.latestWindows.version }}){% endif %}. Price: {% include "components/loom-price.njk" %}. 14-day free trial with every feature unlocked.

